Rule 1 (Length of broadcast dimensions must equal the number of dimensions of the operand tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= v_2.len = ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (Each broadcast dimension must be a valid dimension index within the target shape)
{v_1 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int), v_2 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2[i] < v_1.len
>>
Rule 3 (Target shape dimensions must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (Broadcast dimensions must be unique to avoid mapping multiple input dimensions to the same output dimension)
{v_1 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : if i ≠ j then v_1[i] ≠ v_1[j]
>>
Rule 5 (Each dimension of the operand must either be 1 or equal to the size of the corresponding target dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int), v_3 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = v_2[v_3[i]] ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1
>>
Rule 6 (The operand dimension count must not exceed the target shape length)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2.len
>>
Rule 9 (Operand dimensions must either equal the corresponding target dimension or be 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int), v_3 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = v_2[v_3[i]]
>>
Rule 12 (For list-based shapes, broadcast_dimensions length must equal operand dimensions and target shape size must be sufficient)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int), v_3 : list(int)} |= v_3.len = ndim(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2.len
>>
Rule 13 (For tuple-based shapes, broadcast_dimensions length must equal operand dimensions and target shape size must be sufficient)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int), v_3 : tuple(int)} |= v_3.len = ndim(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2.len
>>
